WEBVTT

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.510
I have been informed that 
Kaito and the others

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:07.290
will be returning to Japan in two days.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.190
Is that right?

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:12.440
On another note, I have received 
word from Director Rook.

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:15.620
He claims to have unraveled the mystery

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:18.100
behind Jin’s behavior 
during his blank year.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.230
Enigma is proving to be 
a tougher nut to crack.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:25.750
Even the POG’s information network 
has been unable to learn anything.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:30.060
Cubik and I are also working 
on the case, but so far...

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:35.720
Hello.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:42.490
Very well. Then we 
shall pay you a visit.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.230
Mr. Principal?

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:48.310
It seems you will get to take

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:50.610
your concerns directly to 
the person in question.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:01:00.760
Now then, let’s enjoy 
a puzzle together,

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:02.700
Lovushka.

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:38.010
Let’s Go to That Place

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:51.270
Your sudden invitation, quite 
honestly, has me speechless.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:55.440
Sorry about that! Believe it 
or not, I’m rather busy.

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:59.670
It’s surprisingly hard to find 
any openings in my schedule.

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:03.280
It has been a while, Jin Makata.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.410
Are you another one of my acquaintances?

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.120
Why the sudden urge to invite them over?

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:15.750
You see, certain people seem to be 
sniffing around my personal affairs.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:18.860
I will be straightforward with you.

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:23.010
I am willing to answer any questions 
you care to throw my way.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:27.180
True, that would make this 
quicker for everyone...

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:29.790
But one thing before we 
start asking questions:

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:34.810
We do not believe that Jin 
has ever hated puzzles.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:36.070
Really?

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:42.950
That statement holds true even if 
he once claimed to hate puzzles.

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:47.050
We believe that he had been 
devoured by the Armlet of Orpheus,

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:50.060
which warped his mind and made 
him say things of that nature.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:54.420
You put up a good argument. 
That is a fascinating theory!

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:57.840
But is that the reality 
of the situation?

00:03:58.350 --> 00:03:59.260
Meaning?

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.210
I have been conducting research 
on the Armlet myself.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:07.600
Admittedly, my research may not 
be as advanced as your own,

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:12.430
but going by past cases, I am 
of the belief that the Armlet

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:15.050
amplifies emotions or 
beliefs that the bearer

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:18.280
already possesses and then warps them.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:22.320
I would love to hear what someone

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.240
who has worn the Armlet 
has to say on the matter.

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:27.240
It sounds logical.

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:30.280
In which case, regardless 
of how great or small,

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:34.840
wouldn’t it be safe to assume 
that Jin Makata possessed

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:37.630
some degree of hatred for puzzles?

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:40.250
That is a possibility.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:47.140
But for an old friend such as myself, 
that is hardly anything new.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:49.970
You’re an... old friend?

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:56.900
Puzzles were always hurting the Jin 
I know, filling him with anguish.

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:02.690
Raetsel, when and where 
did you meet Jin?

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:07.960
He met her while on his pilgrimage 
of Puzzles of Fools...

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:11.680
I’ve heard that it was off 
in a small, mountain village.

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:23.940
What a beautiful puzzle!

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:30.940
That was Raetsel.

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:35.030
She had lost her parents in an accident.

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:39.950
With the help of her neighbors, 
she was managing on her own.

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:48.090
Her parents had given her puzzles 
ever since she was a wee lass.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:52.010
W-would you like to see this one, too?

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:57.870
Did you make it?

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:04.380
She possessed astonishing 
potential as a puzzler.

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:08.320
It was simply a matter 
of time before the POG--

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:11.560
Count Pythagoras--set his sights on her.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:16.300
As such, Jin decided to have Raetsel

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:18.890
travel with him for her own safety.

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:28.670
With no family to turn to, 
she opened her heart to Jin.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:31.030
I’ve heard that she was 
happy to accompany him.

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:35.290
That’s right. Jin, you...

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:42.260
You tried so hard to 
prevent me from seeing...

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:45.310
your harsh battles with 
the Puzzles of Fools.

00:06:49.310 --> 00:06:50.250
But...

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:17.370
Raetsel!

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:27.210
I’m sorry. I scared you 
back there, didn’t I?

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:30.340
No. I wasn’t crying 
because I was scared.

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:32.690
I was crying because I 
felt bad for you, Jin.

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:34.340
Because I wanted to offer you help

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:35.680
when you were out getting 
hurt by yourself...

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:43.490
I couldn’t stand the 
puzzles that tormented you.

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:47.460
That’s why I wanted 
to be there for you!

00:07:58.670 --> 00:07:59.720
Jin!

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:01.400
Jin! Are you okay?

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:05.330
Y-yeah, it’s nothing...

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:09.540
Puzzles are still tormenting you,

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:12.150
just like they did back then.

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:17.850
Jin?

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:22.980
Before I got here, someone attempted 
this Puzzle of Fools, but...

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:34.140
Stop it! That puzzle is a--!

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:39.210
Who are you? Why are you...?

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:42.380
Jin!

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:46.390
What’s wrong?! Hang in there, Jin!

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:55.010
After that, you left Raetsel to 
face Count Pythagoras in battle.

00:08:57.020 --> 00:09:00.680
And then you lost your memories 
and were taken captive.

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:05.960
But Jin entrusted me 
with a certain mission.

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:07.650
A mission?

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:11.460
If anything were to happen to Jin,

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:14.330
I was to gather a group of people 
who would inherit his will

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:16.910
and see his ambitions realized.

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:18.500
Jin’s will...

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:22.540
Are you referring to 
annihilating all puzzlers?

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:25.460
By releasing the Puzzle of God,

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:27.350
obtaining the Book of 
God and using that,

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:31.670
Jin had planned on destroying all 
of the puzzlers in the world.

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:34.170
There aren’t any records to back that.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:37.440
Everything I know about Raetsel 
came directly from Jin.

00:09:38.150 --> 00:09:41.820
I pinpointed her location 
and explained my plan.

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:44.480
Naturally, she offered her approval,

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:47.870
regardless of the fact 
that he told her that

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:50.230
she’s lacking something 
and left her behind.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:57.080
I have genuine admiration for the 
loyalty Raetsel feels toward Jin.

00:10:00.590 --> 00:10:03.780
President, I would 
like to ask a question

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:05.960
about you instead of Raetsel.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:07.120
What might that be?

00:10:07.930 --> 00:10:11.000
Where precisely did you meet Jin?

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:14.480
Back when he was still with the POG,

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:18.260
I just so happened to visit Japan.

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:23.990
Jin has never once mentioned a 
friend that fits your description.

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:28.270
He told me all about you, Baron Kaidou.

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:32.270
Once your puzzles became 
too easy for him,

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:35.950
he decided to start challenging 
the Puzzles of Fools.

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:37.780
You even know about that...?

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:43.990
Tell me: Why did Jin entrust 
you with the Master Brains?

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:48.410
Why did he choose someone who has 
absolutely nothing to do with puzzles?

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:55.550
Do you bear some sort of grudge 
against puzzles as well?

00:11:02.610 --> 00:11:05.790
Puzzles are made to hurt 
people and take lives.

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:09.450
Do I need a special reason to hate them?

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:12.700
Any other questions?

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:18.050
I have one last question. Raetsel?

00:11:18.680 --> 00:11:19.320
What is it?

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:24.200
I’ll admit, Jin definitely harbored 
some uncertainty toward puzzles.

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:26.570
He may have been suffering.

00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:30.690
But when he was with you,

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:33.710
I’m sure he also tried to 
teach you the joy of puzzles.

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:37.230
The Jin I know was that type of guy.

00:11:37.850 --> 00:11:39.630
He showed me their fun side...

00:11:40.480 --> 00:11:43.720
But I hate the puzzles 
that made Jin suffer--

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:45.100
that stole Jin from me!

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:49.360
And once I’ve gotten rid 
of all the puzzlers...

00:11:51.450 --> 00:11:52.600
What then?

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:55.960
I will completely drop puzzles!

00:11:56.580 --> 00:11:59.860
Jin--Jin told me to, so I will!

00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:01.110
He did?

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:08.740
Raetsel,

00:12:09.610 --> 00:12:12.500
you’re free to abandon puzzles.

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:17.530
He told you to abandon puzzles?

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:20.510
Did Jin really say that?

00:12:21.270 --> 00:12:22.170
Master Rook?

00:12:22.810 --> 00:12:23.800
I did...

00:12:26.190 --> 00:12:31.260
I’m sure I said that you’re 
free to abandon puzzles...

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:36.410
It was at night... The 
sound of waves...?

00:12:37.030 --> 00:12:39.320
The beach... We were on the beach...

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:40.440
Jin!

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:43.830
You got another memory back!

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:44.960
I knew it!

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:47.560
I knew I was the only 
one who could help you

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:48.990
get your memories back.

00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:52.750
Jin--Jin, you need me!

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:54.370
Jin!

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:06.730
So that’s what happened...

00:13:07.110 --> 00:13:12.490
But to think that Jin asked 
Enigma to kill all puzzlers...

00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:14.350
I still don’t buy it!

00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:17.410
He said that he would answer 
any of our questions, but...

00:13:17.410 --> 00:13:19.230
Enigma is trying to hide something.

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:23.590
Furthermore, there is nothing 
to back any of his claims.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:26.610
So all we can do is help Jin-Jin 
remember what happened.

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:28.490
I’ve tried everything.

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:31.740
For all of my methods 
to prove ineffective...

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:33.500
What does it mean?

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:37.560
Normal means may not work.

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:39.060
Why not?

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:40.950
Think about it.

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:44.130
How did Jin lose his 
memories to begin with?

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:45.630
The Puzzle of God!

00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:49.320
The Puzzle of God is released when 
two Phi-Brains confront each other.

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:51.500
One gets to obtain the Book of God,

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:55.640
which contains all of our 
world’s natural laws.

00:13:57.620 --> 00:14:02.410
Jin once fought Count Pythagoras 
in the Puzzle of God.

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:04.360
They each paid dearly.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:07.860
It shortened the Count’s life 
and Jin lost his memories.

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:11.770
As for the Book of God that 
was obtained in that battle...

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:14.520
The Puzzle of God and the Book of God...

00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:20.040
They may contain the key to helping 
Jin regain his lost memories.

00:14:20.470 --> 00:14:23.550
The Puzzle of God and the Book of God...

00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:28.140
I never thought I’d hear those 
names come up after all this time.

00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:30.990
I’m sure it isn’t over yet...

00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:34.750
We are still trapped inside 
of the Puzzle of God.

00:14:38.530 --> 00:14:40.330
What possessed you to do that?

00:14:40.330 --> 00:14:41.860
I’m sorry!

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:46.320
With Jin still unable to remember his 
past, I couldn’t help myself...

00:14:46.670 --> 00:14:48.690
I am the one who is supposed to defeat

00:14:48.690 --> 00:14:51.600
Kaito Daimon and help Jin 
recover his memories.

00:14:52.050 --> 00:14:53.200
That was the deal.

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:57.010
You have my sincerest 
apologies, Raetsel.

00:14:57.300 --> 00:14:59.190
This is hard on me, too.

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:03.210
I revere Jin Makata, yet I am 
unable to do anything for him...

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:03.960
It’s hard...

00:15:04.180 --> 00:15:07.440
At any rate, if you’re going 
to keep doing your own thing,

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:09.090
I’ve got an idea of my own.

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:18.980
He remembered something!

00:15:19.240 --> 00:15:21.530
He recovered another memory!

00:15:24.120 --> 00:15:25.480
Yay!

00:15:33.210 --> 00:15:36.220
“Revere”? Me, revere him?

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:40.870
I revere Jin Makata?

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:58.030
That shall be all for today.

00:15:58.610 --> 00:16:00.090
Puzzles are such a rare treat.

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:05.200
I need to take this one slower, 
savoring every moment of it.

00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:13.390
It was simple, yet strong.

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:16.870
And... it was a warm puzzle.

00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:20.590
This is a puzzle that you made.

00:16:21.050 --> 00:16:24.970
Use this Puzzle of Fools, created 
by none other than Jin Makata!

00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:27.720
Jin!

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:31.050
What’s the matter?

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:34.800
Hearing what that Enigma 
guy said about me

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:36.680
didn’t stir any of my memories.

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:39.260
Don’t beat yourself up about it.

00:16:40.400 --> 00:16:43.950
But I made a promise with Kaito.

00:16:44.530 --> 00:16:46.500
I swore that I would bring back

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:48.260
the Jin Makata who taught him puzzles.

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:50.820
That this would be my personal 
battle from here on out.

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:54.570
But you did remember one 
thing, didn’t you?

00:17:01.590 --> 00:17:03.210
That old fart’s a nuisance!

00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:04.790
I remembered something?

00:17:05.550 --> 00:17:08.450
That’s right. “You’re 
free to abandon puzzles.”

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:11.620
Did you honestly tell that to Raetsel?

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:14.660
I honestly think I did.

00:17:15.610 --> 00:17:16.970
Is there a problem with that?

00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:20.220
Well, I find that to be a bit strange.

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:26.600
Long ago, you said something else 
to Kaito when he was still young.

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:30.110
Having lost his parents and all hope,

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:33.740
Kaito was ready to abandon puzzles, 
which were his emotional support.

00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:36.380
Don't give up what is dear.

00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:38.120
Never.

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:43.430
And yet you told Raetsel that 
she may abandon puzzles.

00:17:44.300 --> 00:17:45.780
Why the discrepancy?

00:17:46.180 --> 00:17:47.640
I’m not sure...

00:17:47.640 --> 00:17:49.380
I don’t remember telling 
that to Kaito, either.

00:17:50.280 --> 00:17:51.000
But...

00:17:51.350 --> 00:17:52.250
But?

00:17:52.850 --> 00:17:54.950
But she’s missing something.

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:57.130
That’s the feeling I get.

00:17:57.870 --> 00:18:00.680
Perhaps the two are connected.

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:03.890
“Something.” What 
is this “something”?

00:18:04.450 --> 00:18:06.220
I’m really not certain...

00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:10.520
In all likelihood, it is 
probably related to puzzles.

00:18:11.080 --> 00:18:15.650
In other words, it is something that 
Kaito has and Raetsel doesn’t.

00:18:17.420 --> 00:18:22.300
I get the feeling that at the 
time, I probably needed Kaito,

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:24.160
who possessed whatever 
that “something” is.

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:28.200
That would explain why you told 
Kaito not to give up puzzles,

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:30.420
yet you told Raetsel the opposite.

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:34.180
I loved puzzles, yet I hated puzzles.

00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:37.860
I guided Kaito, yet I abandoned Raetsel.

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:43.500
Jin Makata,

00:18:44.460 --> 00:18:48.290
who in the world were you?

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:00.210
It’s a lie!

00:19:01.340 --> 00:19:02.190
He was lying!

00:19:02.460 --> 00:19:06.000
Jin... needed Kaito more 
than he needed me?!

00:19:06.180 --> 00:19:08.520
More than me... More than me?!

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:09.520
That’s not true!

00:19:16.850 --> 00:19:19.310
He was lying! Lying...

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:24.440
That’s a lie!

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:40.900
No...

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:43.370
No...!

00:19:44.510 --> 00:19:45.690
No!

00:19:46.420 --> 00:19:48.010
Jin belongs to me.

00:19:48.970 --> 00:19:51.420
I will never...

00:19:52.470 --> 00:19:54.050
ever let someone else have him!

00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:05.180
Raetsel!

00:20:05.990 --> 00:20:08.430
Let’s leave together, Jin.

00:20:08.860 --> 00:20:11.490
Together? Right now?

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:13.940
Where would we go?

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:16.800
To a place that only 
you and I know about.

00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:18.570
That’s where we’ll go...

00:20:19.540 --> 00:20:24.130
If you go there, I’m sure all of 
your memories will come flooding back.

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:29.500
Come on! Let’s go, Jin.

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:36.770
Jin has gone missing?!

00:20:37.310 --> 00:20:39.410
I have already contacted the POG.

00:20:39.410 --> 00:20:41.730
They have begun searching for him.

00:20:41.730 --> 00:20:43.020
What should I do?!

00:20:43.020 --> 00:20:44.770
And here I promised 
Kaito I’d protect him.

00:20:44.770 --> 00:20:46.320
I-I’ve gotta find him.

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:49.140
Iwashimizu, prepare to 
launch the mechanic bugs!

00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:52.240
<i>Roger! Catapult: Preparations complete.</i>

00:20:54.910 --> 00:20:56.490
Calm down, Cubik.

00:20:56.490 --> 00:20:57.580
But--!

00:20:57.580 --> 00:20:58.770
Guys!

00:20:59.370 --> 00:21:03.330
This fella said that he 
saw Jin-Jin go bye-bye.

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:07.030
Was he by himself?

00:21:09.050 --> 00:21:10.040
Actually...

00:21:10.420 --> 00:21:11.480
Find him!

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:15.620
Increase the intelligence 
department’s forces and find Jin Makata!

00:21:18.390 --> 00:21:19.420
Raetsel...!

00:21:19.980 --> 00:21:21.190
Mew!

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:24.880
Didn’t I warn you? I said 
I had an idea of my own.

00:21:25.690 --> 00:21:28.010
Isn’t this in violation 
of our contract?

00:21:28.360 --> 00:21:29.920
Is it really?

00:21:30.400 --> 00:21:33.070
Now then, where is Jin?

00:21:34.070 --> 00:21:37.560
Wanna know, Mr. President?

00:21:38.700 --> 00:21:39.900
You damn feral cat!

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:44.900
What?! What’s going on?

00:21:45.290 --> 00:21:46.710
I don’t know!

00:21:46.710 --> 00:21:49.880
All I know is that Raetsel grabbed 
Jin and took off with him.

00:21:50.510 --> 00:21:52.540
Damn that unlucky black cat!

00:21:53.090 --> 00:21:56.550
Freecell and Pinochle are getting 
our plane tickets as we speak--

00:21:58.170 --> 00:21:59.420
Unknown Caller

00:22:01.100 --> 00:22:01.910
Who is it?

00:22:02.310 --> 00:22:03.920
It’s me. Recognize my voice?

00:22:05.100 --> 00:22:05.920
Raetsel!

00:22:07.310 --> 00:22:09.680
Brat! What are you gonna do with Jin?!

00:22:10.860 --> 00:22:12.320
You can be so rude!

00:22:13.040 --> 00:22:14.430
This is a puzzle.

00:22:14.910 --> 00:22:16.570
I am the Giver.

00:22:16.570 --> 00:22:18.060
You are the Solver.

00:22:18.660 --> 00:22:20.060
And the prize is...

00:22:20.700 --> 00:22:21.940
Jin Makata.

00:22:23.760 --> 00:22:26.210
I dare you to solve this puzzle!

00:22:26.210 --> 00:22:28.460
Try to find the two of us!

00:24:02.050 --> 00:24:04.970
I can’t believe you’re making the 
genius basketball player Gammon Sakanoue

00:24:04.970 --> 00:24:05.980
practice nothin’ but the baby basics!

00:24:05.980 --> 00:24:07.480
Dribble 500 times on both 
your left and right.

00:24:07.480 --> 00:24:08.770
Start over if you lose the ball.

00:24:08.770 --> 00:24:11.110
I don’t have time for 
this, Coach Nonoha!

00:24:11.110 --> 00:24:13.650
I need to practice my 
dunks, not dribbling!

00:24:13.650 --> 00:24:16.780
Moron! You’ll never win if you 
haven’t mastered the basics.

00:24:16.780 --> 00:24:19.070
Next time, “What is 
Your Real Dream?”

00:24:17.370 --> 00:24:27.980
What is Your Real Dream?

00:24:19.070 --> 00:24:21.280
And then I’ll make 
my pan-American debut.

00:24:21.280 --> 00:24:23.280
Naturally, it’ll be puzzle novelist.

00:24:23.280 --> 00:24:24.700
The game’s over.

00:24:24.700 --> 00:24:26.070
I wanna play basketball.

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Here is the prize!
Say what?!

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Fin Art: Akeru Otsuki
